When the user pastes `javascript:alert(1)` into `<input type="url">` in the link dialog, `checkValidity()` passes, and Trix accepts it!

Now this is a huge realization!
In Trix toolbar link dialog:
`<input type="url" name="href" ...>`
When the user pastes `javascript:alert(1)` into this link field, HTML5 `<input type="url">` considers `javascript:alert(1)` to be a valid URL.
So `input.checkValidity()` returns `true`!
And `ToolbarController` takes `input.value` (`javascript:alert(1)`) and applies it as the `href` attribute!

